# Datsun Cherry E10 two-door saloon, 1971-1977 (sold in Britain as the Datsun 100A).
#
# The first front-wheel-drive Datsun and the car that established the marque in
# Britain: launched in Japan in October 1970, on sale in Britain from 1971, and
# the model whose owners gave Datsun the highest "would buy another" score in
# Motor's February 1973 reader survey, ahead of the Volkswagen Beetle.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Cherry
#
# Dimensions 3.660 x 1.490 x 1.380 m, wheelbase 2.335 m, from the English
# Wikipedia first-generation (E10) dimension box.
#
# Colours. No UK colour card for the E10 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names rather than invented marketing names: white, red, blue and
# yellow, the four finishes common on 1970s Japanese imports and all four
# visible in period British photographs of the car. Weights white 3, red 3,
# blue 2, yellow 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 130 km/h for the 1.0-litre 100A, the volume British model; the 1.2-litre
# 120A was quicker but rare here. Comfort 50/255, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 50,
# the same as the Fiesta Mk1 and Metro Mk2. Classes 0,1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 1971 intro, retires staggered 1984-1987 on a
# thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-e10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-e10.dae (45 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-cherry-e10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitation: none of the four photographs is a true side profile. The
# proportions were taken from oblique views and calibrated against the published
# dimensions rather than measured off the pictures, so the roofline is a little
# more curved than the car. At 128 px the round lamps in the black grille, the
# chrome bumpers and the two-door outline read correctly.

obj=citycar
name=Datsun100A(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1971
intro_month=1
retire_year=1987
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=0,1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=50
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=255

